18T17:13:14Z"},"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-05-29T11:53:25Z","updated_at":"2025-08-04T17:28:48Z","closed_at":"2025-08-04T17:08:38Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Linux Mint 22.1 (Xia) on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated AMD Radeon Graphics (RADV RENOIR) - AMD Ryzen 7 4800H with Radeon Graphics (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe gizmo to orientate view in 3D editor hides mouse as intended, but if at the same time a popup is triggered, the mouse is left hidden until escape is pressed.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a project and open a 3D scene\n- Open the 3D view\n- With an external editor, change a file so that it triggers a reimport popup next time Godot is focused.\nexample : with a text editor, add an empty line to project.godot so that the file is changed but is still valid\n- To focus Godot, directly click on the orientate view gizmo.\nFor this you must have godot opened in the background and not focus it with alt-tab or workspace change\n- The popup opens, in this example asking for reload but bug still happens for non interactive reload such as assets reimports\n\nIf a camera is present on the scene, it can make it worse as pressing enter to validate project reload will enter preview mode as the same time and escape will no longer make mouse reappear\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[issue.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20503900/issue.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","u